# Next.js & React Patterns

## Server vs client

```tsx
// ✅ Server (default) — no "use client", no hooks
export default function ArticlesPage() {
  return <ArticlesTable data={mockArticles} />
}

// ✅ Client — only when interactive
"use client"
export function AddSourceForm() {
  const [url, setUrl] = useState("")
  return <Input value={url} onChange={(e) => setUrl(e.target.value)} />
}
```

## Rules

- Export `metadata` from server `page.tsx` when titles/SEO matter.
- Use `PageHeader` on `(platform)` pages; pass toolbar actions via `actions`.
- Navigate with `next/link`; active sidebar via `isActivePath()` in `src/lib/navigation.ts`.

## Do not

- Mark full pages `"use client"` when only a child needs interactivity.
- Import `prisma` or read secrets in client components.
- Hardcode API keys — use `process.env` on the server only.
